                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. человек, сражавшийся в рядах белой гвардии во время гражданской войны в России"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5d082b0-fc7a-4e00-ab6b-2fedcc84b232",
                                "sense_id": "900700a6-c1f3-3bc1-9d8d-3ffecf52d599",
                                "text": "Белогвардейцы и красногвардейцы."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "224d97bc-140c-47bc-9b2b-29a423426fbf",
                        "source_entry_id": "dda58590-f91f-3008-a3d2-c42d134c018b",
                        "source_sense_id": "900700a6-c1f3-3bc1-9d8d-3ffecf52d599",
                        "target_lang_word": "White Russian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "White Russian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6131ab3-d8ad-39f0-8413-50453d2b0b8a",
                                        "entry_id": "904631db-6de7-3f6a-a0be-907608065779",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to Russians with tsarist or anti-Soviet sympathies in the period directly following the Revolution in 1917."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba4b0ba0-33ad-4277-9c2f-a49621c5f7c0",
                                                "sense_id": "d6131ab3-d8ad-39f0-8413-50453d2b0b8a",
                                                "text": "The overseer of the clinic was a White Russian woman, a nun, formerly of the Russian Orthodox community in Jerusalem, but a good-hearted woman. In these cases, we should not be too scrupulous politically, said the priest."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e665a5f2-a50f-36ad-af54-d5ca9148c318",
                                        "entry_id": "904631db-6de7-3f6a-a0be-907608065779",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to Belarus, literally \\\"White Russia\\\", or its language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "White Russian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6382936-8919-3418-b1e7-8881a3dacef4",
                                        "entry_id": "3132e065-d57c-3193-81b0-dd6b0184ffbc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cocktail consisting of coffee liqueur, vodka, and milk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31f53849-44bb-4dc8-96c8-f0bad82affd1",
                                                "sense_id": "e6382936-8919-3418-b1e7-8881a3dacef4",
                                                "text": "Few cocktails include milk and cream, so the White Russian is a welcome departure from the norm. Already a popular drink in its own right, the White Russian was made famous by Jeff Bridges’ character in “The Big Lebowski.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cf46538-27e4-3a83-8dc5-204794947ae0",
                                        "entry_id": "3132e065-d57c-3193-81b0-dd6b0184ffbc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A White Guardist, a Russian who did not support the Socialists in the Revolution in 1917 and the Russian Civil War (1917–1923), and afterwards (e.g. as a White émigré)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "595f1fe5-283a-4145-aa68-1441b820b470",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf46538-27e4-3a83-8dc5-204794947ae0",
                                                "text": "The White Guard colony in Harbin is armed and organized along military lines. At the head of this army of counter-revolution—the shock troops of Japanese imperialism—stands the notorious tsarist bandit, \"Ataman\" Semionov."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d02cc3a6-fb11-3322-be60-3d26eaf18960",
                                        "entry_id": "3132e065-d57c-3193-81b0-dd6b0184ffbc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Belarusian person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
